---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const timeline = [
  { week: 'Week 1-2', phase: 'Audit & strategy', desc: 'VITAL audit scored 38/100. Critical gaps: site speed (Lighthouse 32), no booking flow, no lead capture beyond a contact form.' },
  { week: 'Week 3-5', phase: 'Site rebuild', desc: 'Complete site rebuild on Astro + Tailwind. Image optimization brought Lighthouse from 32 to 94. Mobile-first redesign.' },
  { week: 'Week 6-8', phase: 'Booking flow', desc: 'Calendly integration for venue visits. 4-step inquiry form with conditional fields. WhatsApp button with pre-filled templates.' },
  { week: 'Week 9-13', phase: 'Local SEO + reviews', desc: 'Google Business Profile overhaul, 47 citations built, review generation system (12 → 4.7★ across 89 reviews).' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Lotus Mahal — Case study"
  description="How we helped Lotus Mahal, a premium wedding venue in Coimbatore, go from VITAL 38 to 71 in 90 days. 3.4x qualified leads, 12 bookings/month, +94% site speed."
  active="/work"
>
  <section class="hero-section relative">
    <div class="container-wide">
      <a href="/work" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-[#888] hover:text-white mb-6">
        <i class="ph-bold ph-arrow-left"></i> All case studies
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4 text-xs mono text-[#888]">
        <span>Wedding venue</span>
        <span>·</span>
        <span>India</span>
        <span>·</span>
        <span>2025</span>
      </div>
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <h1 class="text-display-1 text-white mb-5">
          Lotus Mahal — inbound booking engine for a <span class="text-gradient-brand">premium venue</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-[#a0a0a0] leading-relaxed mb-6 max-w-2xl">
          A premium wedding venue in Coimbatore rebuilt their website as a booking-first
          experience. Site speed went from Lighthouse 32 to 94. Bookings went from "whenever
          someone DMs" to 12 qualified bookings per month. All on autopilot.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          {['Local SEO', 'Booking flow', 'Performance', 'Reviews'].map((t) => (
            <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-[#1a1a1a] border border-[#2a2a2a] text-xs mono text-[#a0a0a0] rounded">{t}</span>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pb-16">
    <div class="container-wide">
      <div class="card p-10 grid md:grid-cols-4 gap-8">
        <div><div class="eyebrow mb-2">VITAL Score</div><div class="text-5xl font-black text-white mb-1">38 → 71</div><div class="text-xs text-emerald-500">+33 points in 90 days</div></div>
        <div><div class="eyebrow mb-2">Qualified leads</div><div class="text-5xl font-black text-white mb-1">3.4x</div><div class="text-xs text-[#666]">in 4 months</div></div>
        <div><div class="eyebrow mb-2">Site speed</div><div class="text-5xl font-black text-white mb-1">+94%</div><div class="text-xs text-[#666]">Lighthouse score</div></div>
        <div><div class="eyebrow mb-2">Bookings</div><div class="text-5xl font-black text-[var(--color-brand)] mb-1">12/mo</div><div class="text-xs text-[#666]">vs. 3-4 before</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-y">
    <div class="container-wide grid lg:grid-cols-[1fr_2fr] gap-12">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow mb-3">Background</div>
        <h2 class="text-display-3 text-white">A venue with a website problem</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-lg text-[#a0a0a0] leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          Lotus Mahal is a premium wedding venue in Coimbatore, Tamil Nadu. They host 60-80
          weddings a year at price points between ₹15L and ₹50L per event. The venue itself
          is stunning — but the website was built in 2018 and never updated.
        </p>
        <p>
          Bookings came almost entirely from Instagram DMs and word-of-mouth. The website got
          traffic, but it didn\'t convert. There was no booking flow, no inquiry form beyond
          a basic contact field, and the site took 8+ seconds to load on mobile.
        </p>
        <p>
          The owner reached out in early 2025 with one goal: "I want couples researching venues
          to actually book a visit. Right now they message me on Instagram, ask a few questions,
          and disappear."
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-y bg-[#0c0c0c]">
    <div class="container-wide grid lg:grid-cols-[1fr_2fr] gap-12">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow mb-3">The problem</div>
        <h2 class="text-display-3 text-white">Three critical leaks</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <p class="text-lg text-[#a0a0a0] leading-relaxed">
          The VITAL audit identified three critical issues. Each was killing conversions
          independently — together, they were a funnel disaster.
        </p>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <div class="card p-5 flex items-start gap-4">
            <i class="ph-bold ph-gauge text-[var(--color-brand)] text-2xl shrink-0"></i>
            <div>
              <div class="font-bold text-white mb-1">8.2 second load time on mobile</div>
              <p class="text-sm text-[#888]">Unoptimized images, no lazy loading, render-blocking scripts. 64% of couples browse on mobile. Most bounced before the hero loaded.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="card p-5 flex items-start gap-4">
            <i class="ph-bold ph-calendar-x text-[var(--color-brand)] text-2xl shrink-0"></i>
            <div>
              <div class="font-bold text-white mb-1">No booking flow at all</div>
              <p class="text-sm text-[#888]">Just a contact form. No calendar. No way to schedule a venue visit. Couples had to wait 4-12 hours for a response, then message back and forth to find a time.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="card p-5 flex items-start gap-4">
            <i class="ph-bold ph-star text-[var(--color-brand)] text-2xl shrink-0"></i>
            <div>
              <div class="font-bold text-white mb-1">3.2 star Google rating with 12 reviews</div>
              <p class="text-sm text-[#888]">Even though the venue was stunning, the thin review profile made couples hesitate. They\'d read two lukewarm reviews and book the safer competitor.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-y">
    <div class="container-wide grid lg:grid-cols-[1fr_2fr] gap-12">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow mb-3">Our approach</div>
        <h2 class="text-display-3 text-white">Built for booking, not browsing</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-6 text-lg text-[#a0a0a0] leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          We rebuilt the site as a booking-first experience. Every page had a clear next step.
          The new site loads in 1.2 seconds, lets couples book a venue visit in under 60 seconds,
          and shows up in local search results for every relevant query.
        </p>
        <div class="card p-6">
          <div class="eyebrow mb-3">What we shipped</div>
          <ul class="space-y-3 text-base">
            <li class="flex gap-3"><i class="ph-bold ph-check text-[var(--color-brand)] mt-1 shrink-0"></i><span>Complete site rebuild on Astro + Tailwind. Image optimization, lazy loading, preconnect hints. Lighthouse score: 94/100 mobile, 98/100 desktop.</span></li>
            <li class="flex gap-3"><i class="ph-bold ph-check text-[var(--color-brand)] mt-1 shrink-0"></i><span>4-step inquiry form with conditional fields (date, guest count, budget tier). Calendly integration for instant venue visit booking.</span></li>
            <li class="flex gap-3"><i class="ph-bold ph-check text-[var(--color-brand)] mt-1 shrink-0"></i><span>Virtual 360° tour embedded on every package page. Reduces "is this place real?" skepticism before they visit.</span></li>
            <li class="flex gap-3"><i class="ph-bold ph-check text-[var(--color-brand)] mt-1 shrink-0"></i><span>WhatsApp click-to-chat with pre-filled templates. Most Indian couples prefer WhatsApp over email — meeting them where they are.</span></li>
            <li class="flex gap-3"><i class="ph-bold ph-check text-[var(--color-brand)] mt-1 shrink-0"></i><span>Google Business Profile overhaul with new photos, posts, and Q&A. 47 local citations built for Coimbatore wedding venue search terms.</span></li>
            <li class="flex gap-3"><i class="ph-bold ph-check text-[var(--color-brand)] mt-1 shrink-0"></i><span>Review generation system: post-event email + WhatsApp asking for Google reviews. 12 → 89 reviews at 4.7★ average in 4 months.</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-y bg-[#0c0c0c]">
    <div class="container-wide">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mb-12">
        <div class="eyebrow mb-4">Timeline</div>
        <h2 class="text-display-2 text-white">13 weeks from <span class="text-gradient-brand">audit to scale</span></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        {timeline.map((t) => (
          <div class="card p-6 grid md:grid-cols-[120px_1fr_2fr] gap-6">
            <div class="text-xs mono text-[var(--color-brand)]">{t.week}</div>
            <div><div class="font-bold text-white">{t.phase}</div></div>
            <p class="text-sm text-[#888] leading-relaxed">{t.desc}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-y">
    <div class="container-wide">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mb-12">
        <div class="eyebrow mb-4">The results</div>
        <h2 class="text-display-2 text-white">Real numbers, <span class="text-gradient-brand">measured honestly</span></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-12">
        <div class="card p-6">
          <div class="text-3xl font-black text-white mb-2">12/month</div>
          <div class="font-bold text-white mb-2">Qualified bookings</div>
          <p class="text-sm text-[#888] leading-relaxed mb-3">Up from 3-4/month. Each booking is a venue visit from a couple with a confirmed wedding date. ~40% convert to signed contracts.</p>
          <div class="text-xs mono text-[#666]">Verified: Calendly + CRM pipeline data</div>
        </div>
        <div class="card p-6">
          <div class="text-3xl font-black text-white mb-2">+94%</div>
          <div class="font-bold text-white mb-2">Lighthouse score</div>
          <p class="text-sm text-[#888] leading-relaxed mb-3">From 32 to 94 on mobile. Largest single contributor to conversion lift. Mobile bounce rate dropped 47%.</p>
          <div class="text-xs mono text-[#666]">Verified: Lighthouse CI, field data via CrUX</div>
        </div>
        <div class="card p-6">
          <div class="text-3xl font-black text-white mb-2">3.4x</div>
          <div class="font-bold text-white mb-2">Qualified leads</div>
          <p class="text-sm text-[#888] leading-relaxed mb-3">From 9/month to 31/month. Lead quality improved too — fewer tire-kickers, more couples with real budgets and dates.</p>
          <div class="text-xs mono text-[#666]">Verified: Form submissions + lead scoring in CRM</div>
        </div>
        <div class="card p-6">
          <div class="text-3xl font-black text-white mb-2">4.7★</div>
          <div class="font-bold text-white mb-2">Google rating</div>
          <p class="text-sm text-[#888] leading-relaxed mb-3">From 3.2★ with 12 reviews to 4.7★ with 89 reviews. The single biggest trust signal for high-ticket wedding decisions.</p>
          <div class="text-xs mono text-[#666]">Verified: Google Business Profile dashboard</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <blockquote class="card p-8 border-l-4 border-[var(--color-brand)] max-w-3xl">
        <p class="text-xl text-white leading-relaxed mb-4 italic">
          "Before Happyranks, I was chasing couples on Instagram. Now they book a visit
          themselves, show up ready to sign, and the reviews keep building. The new site
          paid for itself in 6 weeks."
        </p>
        <div class="text-sm">
          <div class="font-bold text-white">Karthik Raman</div>
          <div class="text-[#888]">Owner, Lotus Mahal</div>
        </div>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-y bg-[#0c0c0c]">
    <div class="container-wide max-w-3xl">
      <div class="eyebrow mb-4">What we learned</div>
      <h2 class="text-display-2 text-white mb-6">The takeaway</h2>
      <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none space-y-4 text-lg text-[#a0a0a0] leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          Lotus Mahal is a local business case study in how VITAL works. The biggest wins
          weren\'t sexy — they were fundamentals. Site speed. A booking flow that actually
          booked. A review strategy that built trust.
        </p>
        <p>
          The lesson: for local businesses, the VITAL dimensions that matter most are
          Transition (booking) and Learning (knowing which channels produce which leads).
          Visibility matters, but it doesn\'t matter as much as making the existing traffic
          convert.
        </p>
        <p>
          Today Lotus Mahal spends 80% of its marketing budget on the channels that produce
          80% of its bookings — and the VITAL audit re-run at day 90 scored 71, up from 38.
          That\'s a system that compounds.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-y relative overflow-hidden">
    <div class="orb-red top-0 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2"></div>
    <div class="container-wide relative text-center">
      <h2 class="text-display-2 text-white mb-6">Could this be <span class="text-gradient-brand">your business?</span></h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-[#a0a0a0] mb-10 max-w-xl mx-auto">Find out with a free VITAL audit. 90 seconds. Real numbers.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-4">
        <a href="/vital-audit" class="btn btn-primary btn-large"><i class="ph-bold ph-lightning"></i>Get my free VITAL audit</a>
        <a href="/work" class="btn btn-ghost btn-large">Read another case study <i class="ph-bold ph-arrow-up-right"></i></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
